  "hostNotes": "Grade generously: anything a well-stocked coastal cafe/general store would sell counts. The Wye General is a cafe-bar, bakery, Italian-leaning deli, greengrocer, mini FoodWorks and the town's post office, so cooked dishes, cocktails and postage all count. Coffee orders collapse into one Coffee entry; brands collapse into their category (all soft drinks, all packet chips, all ice creams except Gaytime, Magnum and icy poles). Traps: petrol (no servo at Wye River; nearest fuel is Lorne or Apollo Bay), fish and chips or counter meals (that is the Wye Beach Hotel across the road), Tatts/lotto and prescriptions (not an outlet or pharmacy). Takeaway slabs and bottle-shop spirits are unconfirmed but the venue is licensed, so accept. Entries noted as unconfirmed (bait, firewood, gas swap, pizza) are the host's call if the room objects."
